contact='''<footer class="card" id="contact"><h2>Contact</h2><p>For professional opportunities, possible collaborations, or a conversation about shared interests.</p><ul class="contact-list"><li><span class="contact-label">Email:</span> <a href="mailto:filipeee0@gmail.com">filipeee0@gmail.com</a></li><li><span class="contact-label">GitHub:</span> <a href="https://github.com/Filipe-Araujo0">Filipe-Araujo0</a></li><li><span class="contact-label">LinkedIn:</span> <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/filipe-da-silva-araujo-08763916a/">Filipe da Silva Araujo</a></li></ul><a class="source-link" href="https://github.com/Filipe-Araujo0/aboutMe">Original site repository</a></footer>'''
def document(content,title,description):
 return f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>{title} · Filipe</title><meta name="description" content="{description}"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/current.css"></head><body><div class="layout"><main class="page">{content}</main></div><aside class="timeline" id="history" aria-label="Version history"><h2 class="timeline-title">Through time</h2><p class="timeline-description">Explore earlier versions of this site and what changed between them.</p><ol class="timeline-list"></ol><div class="timeline-bottom"><a href="/">Latest version</a></div></aside><button class="history-toggle" aria-controls="history" aria-expanded="false">History</button><script defer src="/timeline.js"></script></body></html>'''
content='''<header class="hero"><h1 class="hero__title">Filipe</h1><p class="hero__eyebrow">Business Analyst &amp; Developer</p><p class="hero__summary">I work with business analysis, financial modeling, and software development, combining analytical thinking with the ability to build tools and put ideas into practice.</p><p class="hero__metadata">São Paulo, Brazil · Updated October 1, 2026</p></header>
<section class="card card-entry" id="about"><h2>About me</h2><p>My background is in mathematics and statistics. I started working with web scraping, data pipelines, and automation, then expanded into internal systems and tools that support operations and decision-making.</p><p>Today, a substantial part of my work is dedicated to business analysis and financial modeling in the real estate sector. I work through assumptions and scenarios, organize information, and translate complex questions into analyses that support decisions.</p><p>Software remains an important part of how I work. My development process is driven by AI agents, with my focus on the purpose of the solution, its design, and the criteria that make it useful and maintainable.</p></section>
<section class="card" id="interests"><h2>What interests me</h2><p>I enjoy learning and understanding how things work: the mechanisms behind a system, the assumptions behind a decision, and the reasons one approach works better than another. That curiosity connects my interests in mathematics, software, finance, and business.</p><p>I'm especially interested in startups and how businesses are built. I want to develop a better understanding of industries, the problems people face, and how to recognize opportunities where technology can create value.</p><p>Cloud computing interests me both for its practical applications and for the architecture that makes computing at scale possible. I'm also curious about how agents, tools, and development environments change the way software is built.</p><p>I like organizing my thoughts and learning with tools such as Todoist, Obsidian, and simple documents. This site's history is another way to keep a record of how my work and interests evolve.</p></section>
<section class="card" id="work"><h2>What I work on</h2><div class="list-columns"><div><h3>Business &amp; finance</h3><ul class="work-list"><li><h3>Business analysis</h3><p>Analyzing business scenarios, organizing information, and assessing assumptions to support decisions.</p></li><li><h3>Financial modeling</h3><p>Building and maintaining models to explore assumptions, scenarios, risks, returns, and financing alternatives.</p></li><li><h3>Decision support</h3><p>Structuring quantitative and qualitative information so that alternatives and trade-offs can be assessed clearly.</p></li></ul></div><div><h3>Software, data &amp; operations</h3><ul class="work-list"><li><h3>Internal systems and automation</h3><p>Building tools that support business operations, improve processes, and organize information.</p></li><li><h3>Data workflows</h3><p>Collecting, processing, and connecting data to make it usable in analyses and day-to-day work.</p></li><li><h3>From requirements to implementation</h3><p>Defining what a solution needs to accomplish and guiding its development with AI agents.</p></li></ul></div></div></section>
<section class="card" id="development"><h2>How I develop software</h2><p>My coding workflow is driven by AI agents and the harnesses that support them: the tools, context, and execution environment in which they work. I guide the implementation by defining the product objective and the standards the solution needs to meet.</p><p>I remain curious about languages and libraries, especially which tools fit a particular problem. My emphasis is on development efficiency, consistency with the project, and code that both people and agents can work with in the future.</p><div class="principles"><article class="principle"><h3>Product purpose &amp; experience</h3><p>Define the product objective and the experience of its users and developers — User Experience (UX) and Developer Experience (DX).</p></article><article class="principle"><h3>Security &amp; performance</h3><p>Establish the security and performance criteria that guide implementation and validation.</p></article><article class="principle"><h3>Organization &amp; documentation</h3><p>Set project structure, conventions, naming, and documentation so that future changes have clear context.</p></article><article class="principle"><h3>Validation &amp; automated tests</h3><p>Choose validation tools and define the behaviors and principles that automated tests should verify.</p></article></div></section>
'''+contact
latest=document(content,'Business Analyst & Developer','Filipe: business analysis, financial modeling, internal tools, and software development driven by AI agents.')
(root/'index.html').write_text(latest)
