changes='''<header class="hero"><h1 class="hero__title">What changed</h1><p class="hero__eyebrow">Version 02 → Version 03</p><p class="hero__metadata">October 1, 2026</p><p class="hero__summary">An updated professional introduction and a return to the visual direction of the original site.</p><div class="version-actions"><a href="/versions/v2/">View version 02</a><a href="/versions/v3/">View version 03</a></div></header><section class="card card-entry"><h2>A clearer professional introduction</h2><div class="compare-grid"><article class="compare-panel"><p class="compare-label">Version 02</p><h3><span class="removed">Software · Data · Curiosity</span></h3><p>The introduction emphasized software and data, with a broad statement about building useful tools.</p></article><article class="compare-panel after"><p class="compare-label">Version 03</p><h3><span class="added">Business Analyst &amp; Developer</span></h3><p>The introduction now includes business analysis and financial modeling alongside software development.</p></article></div></section><section class="card"><h2>How the work is represented</h2><div class="compare-grid"><article class="compare-panel"><p class="compare-label">Before</p><h3>Tools and technologies</h3><p>Lists of languages, frameworks, and libraries were a central part of the presentation.</p></article><article class="compare-panel after"><p class="compare-label">Now</p><h3>Responsibilities and working principles</h3><p>The page explains business analysis, financial modeling, internal systems, and data, together with an AI agent driven development process.</p></article></div><p style="margin-top:1.2rem">The development section covers product purpose, user and developer experience, security, performance, project organization, documentation, naming, validation, and the principles verified by automated tests.</p></section><section class="card"><h2>Curiosity and learning, earlier in the page</h2><p>The interests section now follows the introduction. It describes a curiosity about how systems and decisions work, alongside an interest in learning how to recognize opportunities and build businesses.</p></section><section class="card"><h2>Back to the original visual direction</h2><p>The rounded light cards, soft shadows, blue-gray gradient, and straightforward typography return from version 01. The timeline remains available so that all three versions can be explored.</p><p>The latest page focuses on a professional introduction and contact information. The projects section is omitted, and the employer is not named.</p></section>'''+contact
change_dir=root/'changes/v2-v3';change_dir.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True);(change_dir/'index.html').write_text(document(changes,'Changes · V02 to V03','What changed in Filipe’s portfolio between versions 02 and 03.'))
